\subsection*{4. Real-world Examples}

Previous sections introduced the tools; this section applies them to
familiar data structures.

\subsubsection*{4.1 Range}

Python's built-in \texttt{range} is re-iterable. A class-based
\texttt{Range} with a generator-returning \texttt{\_\_iter\_\_} matches
that behavior: each call to \texttt{iter(c)} produces a fresh
generator, so the container can be looped over many times.

Contrast with a class that stores a single generator instance: that
class is one-shot, like the generator itself.
